# The Include lines sit at top level, ahead of any Host stanza, because that is
# the only position where the included stanzas actually activate. Verified
# against OpenSSH_10.3p1: with `Include included/*` placed inside the
# `Host local-one` stanza instead, `ssh -G from-include` reports
# `hostname from-include` / `user operator` — the included stanza is parsed under
# NEVERMATCH and never applies. Hoisted above `Host local-one`, the same
# `ssh -G from-include` reports `hostname 10.2.2.2` / `user included-user`.
Include included/*

Include ./missing/nothing-here

Host local-one
  HostName 10.1.1.1

Host local-two
  HostName 10.1.1.2
